## Description

This detection identifies the execution of common Windows network discovery commands that attackers frequently use during the **Discovery** phase of an intrusion.

After gaining access to a system, adversaries typically enumerate the network configuration, active connections, DNS information, and reachable hosts before moving laterally. Monitoring these commands enables defenders to detect reconnaissance activity early in the attack lifecycle.

