# Analyst Notes

Network discovery is one of the earliest stages of an attack after initial access. Threat actors commonly gather information about IP addresses, DNS configuration, active network connections, and reachable systems before attempting privilege escalation or lateral movement.

Although these utilities are legitimate Windows tools, monitoring their execution provides valuable visibility into reconnaissance behavior and should be correlated with authentication events, PowerShell activity, scheduled task creation, and service modifications for improved detection accuracy.
